WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.438 --> 00:00:02.607
Where is purgatory in the Bible?

2
00:00:02.607 --> 00:00:04.031
The word isn't there.

3
00:00:04.031 --> 00:00:05.930
Neither is the word Trinity.

4
00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.371
The question is whether the idea is.

5
00:00:08.821 --> 00:00:10.991
Start with what purgatory isn't.

6
00:00:10.991 --> 00:00:14.652
It isn't a second chance, and it isn't a halfway hell.

7
00:00:14.652 --> 00:00:18.924
The Catechism says it's for people who die in God's friendship,

8
00:00:18.924 --> 00:00:22.924
already assured of heaven, who still need to be made clean.

9
00:00:22.924 --> 00:00:26.111
Nothing unclean enters heaven, says Revelation.

10
00:00:26.561 --> 00:00:27.578
Now Saint Paul.

11
00:00:27.578 --> 00:00:29.409
In First Corinthians three,

12
00:00:29.409 --> 00:00:33.002
each person's work is tested by fire on the last day.

13
00:00:33.002 --> 00:00:37.477
If it burns, "he shall suffer loss: but he himself shall be saved,

14
00:00:37.477 --> 00:00:41.342
yet so as by fire." Saved, and still something to suffer.

15
00:00:41.342 --> 00:00:42.902
That's the shape of it.

16
00:00:43.352 --> 00:00:44.979
And in Second Maccabees,

17
00:00:44.979 --> 00:00:51.217
Judas Maccabeus has a sacrifice offered for fallen soldiers so they might be freed from sin.

18
00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:55.150
Praying for the dead only makes sense if it can help them.

19
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.752
That's purgatory.

20
00:00:56.752 --> 00:00:57.837
Not God's anger.

21
00:00:57.837 --> 00:00:59.871
God finishing what he started.
